      "message": "fix(post): refuse an upright section after a tilt without uprightReturn\n\nA post script of the user (PostRef::File) had no law that makes it\nstate the return of the rotaries. An operation that follows a tilted\noperation and states no angle then cut at the old lean, and no check\nstopped it.\n\n- New manifest flag uprightReturn = true: the script retracts and\n  commands the rotaries to zero at the start of each section that\n  follows a tilted section.\n- New engine pass post::upright_after_tilt: when the script does not\n  declare the flag, a section whose first move states no A/B/C after a\n  section that left a rotary off zero is refused by name (a counted\n  warning, which blocks the post).\n- fanuc, doosan-dnm, mach4 and tormach declare the flag. Each has a\n  posting test of the real order in upright_after_tilt.rs.\n- The Mach4 AC trunnion fixture moves to tests/ac_trunnion_support so\n  that upright_after_tilt.rs can pin Mach4.\n\nFixes #3477\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
